* Frostner can also be upgraded at the [[Forge of Potential]] with a [[Silver Battle Idol]].

== Notes ==
* The [[Damage types#Frost|Frost]] damage is applied instantly, even though the slow persists over time.
* The [[Damage types#Spirit|Spirit]] damage is applied over time (and only affects some enemies).
* The hammer itself also gives off a Frost Aura, which is a purely visual effect.
* The [[Wet Effect|Wet]] status causes Frost weakness, making the Frostner effective against enemies submerged in water (rain only affects players).
* Players are less likely to see a foe stagger from damage from Frostner compared to other maces; this is because frost does not contribute to [[Stagger|staggering]], only physical damage does.
* The knockback can be detrimental when focusing a target down, especially when playing in a group. Using the secondary attack to finish off the target may be preferred over primary attacks. 
* The combination of knockback and slowing effect provided by frost makes the Frostner optimal for crowd control. 

== Trivia ==
* Frostner's appearance is loosely based on archeological finds and artistic representations of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mj%C3%B6lnir Mjölnir], the one-handed hammer of Thor.

